{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/860928-dreams-of-avarice-and-the-beloved-of-justice","id":860928,"title":"Dreams of Avarice and the Beloved of Justice","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-07T04:05:12-07:00","id":860928,"title":"Dreams of Avarice and the Beloved of Justice","content":"Obviously, contains references to Dreams of Avarice. If you consider it as a spoiler, please stop reading right here :P<br /> <br /> So, as we all know, hunters has a very disturbing tendency to work with the &quot;natural predators&quot; of their enemies. That tendency shows up usually among Conspiracies, with some is more obvious, like the Les Mysteres and the Knights of St Adrian, while in others it is more open for interpretations, like the Knights of St George and the Cainte Heresy. While the big players in the Vigil suffer from this phenomena more than the small powers, Compacts also sometimes ends up being connected to the monsters of monsters- Division VI serve the Seers, the Illuminated Brotherhood is touched by the Shadow, the Maiden Blood's Sisterhood works with witches and blood magic. And yet, among all of those shaded groups, there are few, seemingly pure and honest hunters who manage to keep their light shining- the Protectors of Light, the Talbot Group, the Habibti Ma.<br /> <br /> But maybe it is not the case.<br /> <br /> Sure, it may just be a bit of paranoia- for example, I still remember how, when Slasher was still young and fresh, people were trying desperately to find some hidden skeleton in their closet, grasping into few paragraphs like the Hall of Mirrors of the one-line description of their Director of Operation who works none-stop simply because everyone believed that conspiracies had to be manipulated by <i>something</i> (I think it was eventually tied to the God Machine with the Director being an Angel from the Pain Prophet's Testament. Never truly understood the train of thought). Of course, this does not have to be the case. People just love to make theories and find villains everywhere. Plus, there is nothing weird about the Habibti Ma. They are nice, truly caring for their friends and family and trying to do something which is, undoubtedly, good.<br /> <br /> And then, there is Dreams of Avarice.<br /> <br /> The Habibti Ma seem nice because they invoke Maa't as their symbol- a being which everyone who know a thing about Ancient Egyptian Religion wouldn't ever think could mean something is wrong with them. Yet, the problem is not the Egyptian Mythology- but the Iremite one. Apparently, Maa't comes from M't, which means Suffering, or Sacrifice. M't is meant to represent the Law of Suffering, the force the Judges use in order to force Sekhem into form and eventually feed the Devourer. Maa't, Lady Justice, is actually Lady Suffering. She is the tyranny of the Judges and the Law they impose upon the world. And the Habibti Maa invoke that name- and as everyone knows, names are very important for the Deathless and the Nameless.<br /> <br /> So- does it mean that the Habibti Maa are manipulated by the highest tyrants of the world? Not necessary- there is no real mechanical benefit which may represent a boon granted by the Judges or their Law to the compact. The only thing which may hint about such connection is that the ones treated by them usually claim that their methods work. It would also make you wander why would the Judges patronize the group, as the Arisen still (usually) serve their purpose at shaping Sekhem according to the Law. Still, the possibility is out there- and who knows what Heavens has in mind for those good heart hunters?<br /> <br /> So- if you were to decide to establish a connection between the Law and the Habibti Maa, how would you do it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T05:57:36-07:00","id":863585,"title":"","content":"A connection need not be sinister. The cruelty of the Judges makes it easy to forget that most of the crimes they want punished still fit modern ideas of what should be criminal. So perhaps the Habibi Ma aren't sponsored by &quot;the Judges,&quot; but by <i>a</i> Judge, specifically the one that punishes abuses of power - the crime that can fairly be said to be the very definition of the cults the compacts oppose. Cults run by the Deathless wouldn't be exempt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}